WEBVTT

00:01.135 --> 00:02.966
Prepare to fire the
anti-proton cannon!

00:05.339 --> 00:07.241
Forward port ready to open!

00:07.241 --> 00:08.265
Opening now!

00:11.445 --> 00:14.141
Numbers 5 and 6, safety released!

00:14.381 --> 00:16.713
Target laser cannons forward!

00:18.285 --> 00:21.652
We have less than twenty seconds
before space-time fusion.

00:29.029 --> 00:32.066
Ten... nine... eight...

00:32.066 --> 00:35.202
...seven... six... five...

00:35.202 --> 00:39.406
...four... three... two... one.

00:39.406 --> 00:40.600
Space-time fusion!

00:47.214 --> 00:48.647
All ships! Attack!

00:56.824 --> 00:58.559
Imperial Calendar Year 955.

00:58.559 --> 01:01.428
The battleships of the
Star Forces...

01:01.428 --> 01:04.431
...had countered the advances
of the Triple Alliance...

01:04.431 --> 01:08.635
...which consisted of
the United Mankind...

01:08.635 --> 01:08.836
...the Republic of Greater Alcont...

01:08.836 --> 01:11.805
Imperial Capital Lakfakalle
...the Republic of Greater Alcont...

01:11.805 --> 01:12.873
Imperial Capital Lakfakalle
...and The People's Sovereign
Union of Planets.

01:12.873 --> 01:15.009
...and The People's Sovereign
Union of Planets.

01:15.009 --> 01:17.637
The counterattack had begun.

01:17.978 --> 01:18.812
As commander of the Third Fleet...

01:18.812 --> 01:20.714
Commander-in-Chief
Commanding Admiral Abriel
As commander of the Third Fleet...

01:20.714 --> 01:25.085
Commander-in-Chief
Commanding Admiral Abriel
...as well as overall
commander-in-chief...

01:25.085 --> 01:26.053
...Commander Abriel amassed
a huge fleet of 150 squadrons.

01:26.053 --> 01:29.923
First Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral Spoor
...Commander Abriel amassed
a huge fleet of 150 squadrons.

01:29.923 --> 01:30.391
First Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral Spoor
Additional forces of
training ships on standby...

01:30.391 --> 01:30.891
Additional forces of
training ships on standby...

01:30.891 --> 01:32.059
Second Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rulef
Additional forces of
training ships on standby...

01:32.059 --> 01:35.496
Second Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rulef
...will provide another seventy
squadrons in the event of a battle.

01:35.496 --> 01:35.963
...will provide another seventy
squadrons in the event of a battle.

01:35.963 --> 01:39.867
Fourth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Kotoponi
...will provide another seventy
squadrons in the event of a battle.

01:39.867 --> 01:40.300
Fourth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Kotoponi
Sparing nothing...

01:40.300 --> 01:41.001
Sparing nothing...

01:41.001 --> 01:45.639
Fifth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rekef
...to reorganize the fleet
in terms of scale...

01:45.639 --> 01:49.943
...training, and top personnel,
the Star Forces have dubbed this...

01:49.943 --> 01:52.878
Operation Phantom Flame.

01:53.313 --> 01:57.875
Now, the battle will truly begin.

02:05.492 --> 02:09.223
The First Campaign

02:15.035 --> 02:19.699
Banner of the Stars

03:44.091 --> 03:47.060
The first group of mines has
been confirmed as destroyed.

03:49.029 --> 03:50.898
Our first orders have
been carried out.

03:50.898 --> 03:52.559
Initiate space-time separation!

03:52.699 --> 03:54.530
Starting space-time separation!

04:02.342 --> 04:04.367
That seemed too easy.

04:04.978 --> 04:07.114
The real battle is starting now!

04:07.114 --> 04:09.316
While we were
watching out for mines...

04:09.316 --> 04:11.284
...the enemy ship has
moved further ahead.

04:11.752 --> 04:14.388
Captain, there's a message
from command.

04:14.388 --> 04:16.379
They want us in
single-column formation.

04:16.523 --> 04:19.126
Senior Aviator.
Single-column formation.

04:19.126 --> 04:20.252
Yes, ma'am.

04:27.935 --> 04:29.903
Our assault ship squadrons...

04:29.903 --> 04:31.996
...are hunting down the enemy
patrol ships one by one.

04:34.041 --> 04:36.532
It's just like that time we were
on the Gosroth...

04:36.977 --> 04:39.411
...although it's the other way around.

04:52.492 --> 04:55.586
But this doesn't mean we're safe.

04:55.796 --> 04:58.731
This time we're at the
forefront of the battle.

04:58.932 --> 05:01.101
If we get out of this
without casualties...

05:01.101 --> 05:02.193
...it'll be a miracle.

05:02.669 --> 05:05.866
It wouldn't surprise me
if we got wiped out.

05:06.039 --> 05:08.030
You can be so negative.

05:10.210 --> 05:12.079
To be totally honest with you...

05:12.079 --> 05:14.877
...I'm extremely scared.

05:16.416 --> 05:18.385
And if I'm honest with you...

05:18.385 --> 05:19.818
...I'm scared, too.

05:20.487 --> 05:23.047
Knowing that makes me
feel better.

05:24.024 --> 05:25.525
How could knowing that
I'm afraid...

05:25.525 --> 05:27.652
...possibly make you feel better?

05:28.128 --> 05:29.891
Well, I wonder why.

05:30.597 --> 05:33.500
If I were to be the only one
trembling in fear...

05:33.500 --> 05:36.492
...it wouldn't be very fair.

05:37.337 --> 05:38.572
Perhaps.

05:38.572 --> 05:41.837
But I don't think there's
anyone here who isn't afraid.

05:42.576 --> 05:44.544
Perhaps with the exception
of your cat.

05:45.379 --> 05:47.814
The only time Diaho's afraid...

05:47.814 --> 05:49.714
...is when it's time for a wash.

05:52.286 --> 05:56.089
The only one on this ship who
has any battle experience...

05:56.089 --> 06:00.127
...is Samson, who survived
the battle at Scaresche Gate...

06:00.127 --> 06:02.152
...three years ago.

06:04.264 --> 06:07.631
We have twelve minutes until
space-time fusion with the enemy!

06:12.639 --> 06:16.473
I can't believe we're seriously
going in for an attack...

06:16.677 --> 06:19.179
...hitting those patrol ships with
our six-ship squadron.

06:19.179 --> 06:22.580
It's beyond brave. It's reckless.

06:22.716 --> 06:25.412
The lead ship Gamroil
has decreased its speed.

06:26.286 --> 06:28.088
What a relief.

06:28.088 --> 06:31.158
For a minute I thought our
six ships were on our own!

06:31.158 --> 06:34.855
I'd say we're holding back so
the other squadrons can catch up.

06:35.495 --> 06:38.896
Good thing the Hecto-Commander
knows what she's doing.

06:39.700 --> 06:42.260
There's been a change to the
schedule for space-time fusion.

06:45.372 --> 06:46.999
The 4th assault unit is approaching!

06:47.274 --> 06:50.377
Transmission received requesting
us to move in parallel formation.

06:50.377 --> 06:52.279
Senior Aviator,
I'll leave that to you.

06:52.279 --> 06:53.337
Yes, ma'am.

06:54.581 --> 06:57.243
New estimate for
space-time fusion...

06:57.918 --> 06:58.885
...ten minutes.

06:59.786 --> 07:03.156
I guess we have to sit tight
for the next ten minutes.

07:03.156 --> 07:03.713
Yes.

07:04.358 --> 07:06.360
2nd and 5th assault units
in space-time fusion...

07:06.360 --> 07:07.725
...with the enemy ship.

07:10.497 --> 07:15.093
It's like a pack of carnivores ready
to pounce on the giant herbivore.

07:15.769 --> 07:17.471
You ever see something like that?

07:17.471 --> 07:19.962
In a documentary,
when I was a child.

07:25.612 --> 07:27.514
Looks like it's over.

07:27.514 --> 07:28.037
Yes.

07:28.448 --> 07:31.518
We suffered casualties but
our side was victorious.

07:31.518 --> 07:33.587
Everyone, it's going to be
our turn next!

07:33.587 --> 07:34.454
Captain!

07:34.454 --> 07:36.523
The enemy ship's space-time
bubble has divided!

07:36.523 --> 07:39.326
There are four. Probably mines.

07:39.326 --> 07:41.027
So, they had some left.

07:41.027 --> 07:42.729
Releasing those remaining mines...

07:42.729 --> 07:45.254
...was probably
an act of desperation.

07:45.432 --> 07:47.423
And what does
Squadron Command say?

07:47.601 --> 07:48.761
We've heard nothing yet.

07:49.870 --> 07:50.837
Here's something.

07:51.405 --> 07:53.440
It's a message from Command.

07:53.440 --> 07:55.242
It says, "Do what you have to do."

07:55.242 --> 07:56.231
I see.

07:57.144 --> 08:01.478
We can't enter space-time fusion
and just wait for them to attack us.

08:02.582 --> 08:03.283
Jinto...

08:03.283 --> 08:05.085
...you shall return to your position.

08:05.085 --> 08:06.520
It's your duty to monitor
the air pressure...

08:06.520 --> 08:09.356
...and treat any casualties
that may result.

08:09.356 --> 08:12.325
But those mines are
headed straight for us.

08:12.325 --> 08:15.362
If we hit even one of them,
we'll be blown to pieces!

08:15.362 --> 08:17.956
I don't think there's
anything I can do.

08:18.565 --> 08:20.066
I suppose that's true.

08:20.066 --> 08:21.635
Well, do what you want.

08:21.635 --> 08:24.204
Just make sure you're
steady on your feet.

08:24.204 --> 08:25.739
If you fall over on top of me...

08:25.739 --> 08:28.264
...and distract me from running
the ship, that'll be the end of us.

08:29.109 --> 08:30.343
I'll be careful.

08:30.343 --> 08:33.005
Space-time bubbles suspected
to be enemy mines approaching!

08:33.313 --> 08:34.881
They've passed Gamroil...

08:34.881 --> 08:36.143
...and are heading this way!

08:36.583 --> 08:37.277
Distance: 5...

08:38.018 --> 08:38.643
...4...

08:39.286 --> 08:40.253
...3.5...

08:40.654 --> 08:41.746
...3.2...

08:41.922 --> 08:43.048
...3. 1...

08:44.624 --> 08:45.522
...3.3.

08:47.060 --> 08:49.688
Enemy space-time bubbles
have passed us!

08:51.431 --> 08:55.231
At least we avoided the shame
of dying in our first battle!

08:55.769 --> 08:57.237
Enemy space-time bubbles!

08:57.237 --> 09:00.070
They're entering space-time
fusion with ships at the rear!

09:01.875 --> 09:03.103
Is it the Leekroil?

09:03.643 --> 09:04.803
It's the Kidroil.

09:09.082 --> 09:11.448
Confirming space-time fusion
with third enemy ship!

09:11.751 --> 09:15.856
Those enemy mines appear
to be attracted to this ship.

09:15.856 --> 09:18.620
Counterattack with laser cannons
as soon as you're ready!

09:18.892 --> 09:21.053
Fire the anti-proton cannon
at the first mine!

09:24.898 --> 09:28.698
Follow that immediately
with the third!

09:43.950 --> 09:45.519
The approach continues!

09:45.519 --> 09:47.919
Space-time fusion with the
sixth ship of the 4th unit!

09:48.255 --> 09:50.323
Calling the Kidroil!
Captain Beikal!

09:50.323 --> 09:52.223
Can you afford to answer me?

09:52.425 --> 09:55.462
Barely in a position
to respond...

09:55.462 --> 09:57.063
...would be more like it.

09:57.063 --> 09:59.429
That's all I wanted to hear.

10:00.934 --> 10:02.424
Survive this!

10:03.970 --> 10:06.461
That last mine is heading
straight for the port side!

10:07.374 --> 10:09.001
Fire the laser cannons!

10:20.587 --> 10:23.857
The sixth ship of the 4th Squadron
has vanished!

10:23.857 --> 10:25.085
The Kidroil?

10:25.292 --> 10:26.657
Checking now.

10:27.394 --> 10:28.952
The action has stopped.

10:29.162 --> 10:30.322
And the Kidroil...

10:32.499 --> 10:33.733
They're fine!

10:33.733 --> 10:34.427
I see.

10:34.634 --> 10:35.566
However...

10:36.636 --> 10:39.730
...they've slowed
down significantly.

10:40.874 --> 10:42.008
Damn!

10:42.008 --> 10:44.067
The remnants of those mines
are too heavy.

10:44.511 --> 10:45.445
Kidroil!

10:45.445 --> 10:48.882
It appears the weight of your
space-time bubble has increased.

10:48.882 --> 10:51.407
I apologize, Commander.

10:51.952 --> 10:53.353
But at this rate...

10:53.353 --> 10:54.721
...we can't keep up with you.

10:54.721 --> 10:56.018
I understand.

10:56.389 --> 10:59.119
But I'm expecting more
from you in the next battle.

11:01.361 --> 11:03.329
The Kidroil is holding back.

11:04.197 --> 11:07.567
Looks like the commander has
no intention of slowing down.

11:07.567 --> 11:10.627
Seven minutes until space-time
fusion with the enemy ship!

11:11.004 --> 11:13.206
That makes it ten of us
against one.

11:13.206 --> 11:14.935
The odds are in our favor.

11:15.408 --> 11:18.275
This is looking more and more
like the Gosroth.

11:18.745 --> 11:21.270
So, we have to win this one.

11:21.715 --> 11:24.115
You truly lack common sense.

11:24.451 --> 11:27.579
There are no battles we fight
that we don't have to win.

11:29.155 --> 11:30.857
I guess you're right about that!

11:30.857 --> 11:33.018
Six minutes to space-time fusion!

11:33.293 --> 11:36.730
Jinto, it's time you return
to your station.

11:36.730 --> 11:37.998
Once we engage that ship...

11:37.998 --> 11:40.023
...there'll be things for you to do.

11:41.368 --> 11:42.596
Of course.

11:47.540 --> 11:49.275
That's strange.

11:49.275 --> 11:50.537
I'm not afraid any more.

11:53.246 --> 11:56.113
Was that why he came on board?

11:57.684 --> 12:00.152
No. That would be
too thoughtful of him!

12:05.725 --> 12:07.560
All of us here on the Basroil...

12:07.560 --> 12:09.596
...will commence the
first phase of battle...

12:09.596 --> 12:11.931
...as soon as we enter into space-
time fusion with the enemy ship.

12:11.931 --> 12:14.365
All crew prepare for battle!

12:21.975 --> 12:23.806
One minute to space-time fusion!

12:24.377 --> 12:25.679
The lead ship Gamroil...

12:25.679 --> 12:27.806
...will reach space-time fusion
in thirty-two seconds.

12:28.248 --> 12:30.850
Establish a communication link
with the Gamroil...

12:30.850 --> 12:32.719
...as soon as we enter
space-time fusion!

12:32.719 --> 12:33.743
Yes, ma'am.

12:43.596 --> 12:45.265
The Gamroil is in
space-time fusion!

12:45.265 --> 12:46.926
We'll be there in fifteen seconds!

12:52.472 --> 12:53.496
Ten seconds!

12:53.773 --> 12:55.709
Nine... eight...

12:55.709 --> 12:57.677
...seven... six...

12:57.677 --> 12:59.579
...five... four...

12:59.579 --> 13:02.716
...three... two... one.

13:02.716 --> 13:04.411
Space-time fusion!

13:17.097 --> 13:19.766
Damn, they've already
destroyed one of ours.

13:19.766 --> 13:21.893
Receiving transmission
from the Gamroil.

13:22.902 --> 13:26.606
Welcome to the battlefield,
Deca-Commander Abriel.

13:26.606 --> 13:28.540
Proceed to your position!

13:28.742 --> 13:29.731
Roger!

13:35.014 --> 13:37.141
They've fired their
laser cannon at us!

13:38.118 --> 13:40.313
Phew! That was close!

13:41.888 --> 13:46.086
Our defensive magnetic shield is
designed to repel laser cannons.

13:46.426 --> 13:49.262
But the ship can
still sustain damage.

13:49.262 --> 13:50.456
Enemy ship ahead!

14:00.306 --> 14:01.775
Direct hit on enemy ship.

14:01.775 --> 14:03.436
But there's only minimal damage.

14:04.577 --> 14:06.513
Now arriving in position!

14:06.513 --> 14:08.982
Now, let's shoot like crazy.

14:08.982 --> 14:10.250
I know that!

14:10.250 --> 14:12.946
Just make sure you monitor
the engines during battle!

14:18.758 --> 14:19.452
Damn!

14:20.360 --> 14:22.988
Even the Princess is
fighting bravely.

14:25.398 --> 14:27.263
We're out of the net.

14:33.072 --> 14:34.941
A ship has been hit by
electromagnetic cannon!

14:34.941 --> 14:36.067
Which one?

14:36.442 --> 14:38.706
The second ship
of the 4th Squadron.

14:39.112 --> 14:40.773
Whether the crew escaped
or not...

14:41.481 --> 14:42.846
...remains unconfirmed.

14:43.416 --> 14:45.475
Now only eight of us are left.

14:46.219 --> 14:48.087
Enemy's laser cannons!

14:48.087 --> 14:49.577
Focused in our direction!

14:50.056 --> 14:52.422
Increase output
of magnetic shield!

15:00.033 --> 15:01.159
Damage report!

15:01.467 --> 15:03.594
Hold 14 was hit.

15:03.837 --> 15:04.929
But I think we're okay.

15:05.104 --> 15:08.130
No one was there,
and it wasn't pressurized.

15:08.308 --> 15:10.176
What do you mean we're okay?

15:10.176 --> 15:13.546
We keep valuable spare parts
for our equipment in that hold.

15:13.546 --> 15:15.515
Hope they haven't been destroyed.

15:15.515 --> 15:18.040
But surely they can be replaced.

15:18.251 --> 15:22.422
Some of those parts
are brand new!

15:22.422 --> 15:25.516
Don't you understand
how painful that is?

15:28.061 --> 15:31.631
So, that's the way our experienced
pilot handles his fear.

15:31.631 --> 15:34.725
Four electromagnetic cannon
shots headed for the Helzroil!

15:35.134 --> 15:36.396
They're going to be hit!

15:38.771 --> 15:41.708
Helzroil, you have permission
to temporarily retreat!

15:41.708 --> 15:43.471
Hurry up and separate!

15:47.614 --> 15:49.514
The Helzroil has been destroyed.

15:49.949 --> 15:51.940
They must've retreated too late!

15:52.619 --> 15:55.088
I can't believe there are
casualties in my squadron!

15:55.088 --> 15:56.988
The enemy ship has
changed direction!

15:58.224 --> 16:00.351
The expected target is...

16:00.894 --> 16:02.020
...the Basroil!

16:04.564 --> 16:07.100
Electromagnetic cannon
targeted on this ship!

16:07.100 --> 16:09.591
Basroil, you have permission
to temporarily retreat!

16:09.836 --> 16:10.564
Lafiel!

16:10.937 --> 16:12.131
Space-time separation!

16:12.705 --> 16:13.729
Hurry up!

16:14.707 --> 16:15.969
We're being attacked!

16:20.480 --> 16:21.504
Looks bad.

16:24.217 --> 16:25.707
Engines, full power!

16:35.128 --> 16:36.595
Fire anti-proton cannon!

17:09.929 --> 17:12.465
Space-time separation
in ten seconds!

17:12.465 --> 17:16.069
Nine... eight... seven... six...

17:16.069 --> 17:20.606
...five... four... three... two... one.

17:20.606 --> 17:22.005
Separation!

17:44.030 --> 17:45.765
We're still alive.

17:45.765 --> 17:47.528
It was close.

17:48.634 --> 17:53.367
Our other ships are space-time
fusing with the enemy ship.

17:55.174 --> 17:57.608
I guess they don't need us now.

18:01.414 --> 18:03.049
Re-enter the space-time bubble!

18:03.049 --> 18:06.348
The commander only gave us
permission to retreat temporarily.

18:06.552 --> 18:07.576
Not a full retreat.

18:07.987 --> 18:08.817
Right away!

18:09.188 --> 18:10.189
Boy, oh, boy...

18:10.189 --> 18:13.420
Couldn't we have just let
the others deal with it?

18:14.694 --> 18:15.786
Space-time fusion!

18:30.943 --> 18:33.713
They don't even have enough
power for their magnetic shield.

18:33.713 --> 18:35.340
It's a massacre.

18:36.215 --> 18:39.185
I don't like to fight this way.

18:39.185 --> 18:41.176
It doesn't matter whether
you like it or not.

18:41.621 --> 18:43.923
Assault ships aren't powerful.

18:43.923 --> 18:47.450
This is the only way we can
fight against a ship like that.

18:47.760 --> 18:50.490
You're right.
I'm sorry, Captain.

18:51.431 --> 18:53.763
We could finish it in one shot.

18:53.933 --> 18:56.128
Basroil, all ships are to retreat.

18:56.803 --> 18:59.533
I'm sorry, considering you
just re-entered the battlefield.

18:59.739 --> 19:01.007
All ships!

19:01.007 --> 19:02.942
Separate from the space-time
bubble immediately!

19:02.942 --> 19:04.143
But why?

19:04.143 --> 19:06.079
We're so close to destroying it!

19:06.079 --> 19:07.180
I know.

19:07.180 --> 19:10.877
However, we received
orders directly from HQ.

19:11.050 --> 19:13.575
The battleship squadron
is ready for action.

19:13.853 --> 19:16.789
They've decided to use mines
to destroy that ship.

19:16.789 --> 19:18.848
Very well. I understand.

19:20.626 --> 19:22.184
Prepare for space-time separation.

19:22.728 --> 19:23.023
Yes, ma'am.

19:24.230 --> 19:26.061
Captain.

19:26.499 --> 19:29.368
They made the right decision.

19:29.368 --> 19:32.004
Even though we nearly
destroyed that patrol ship...

19:32.004 --> 19:36.065
...we might've risked losing a few
more ships along with it.

19:36.509 --> 19:41.276
It's more prudent to use mines
which don't result in casualties.

19:42.415 --> 19:43.541
Space-time separation!

19:44.784 --> 19:47.014
Mine attacks have
now commenced.

19:49.655 --> 19:51.213
It's so over-the-top.

19:58.364 --> 20:00.264
Enemy ship has been destroyed.

20:04.537 --> 20:09.634
The Assault Ship Squadron is simply for
keeping the enemy at bay.

20:13.212 --> 20:13.837
Captain...

20:15.248 --> 20:16.883
...we should have ourselves a drink.

20:16.883 --> 20:18.584
And have a toast.

20:18.584 --> 20:20.019
A toast?

20:20.019 --> 20:22.221
Even though we didn't
win the battle?

20:22.221 --> 20:24.223
That's not the point!

20:24.223 --> 20:27.056
It's that we all survived
our first battle.

20:29.028 --> 20:29.892
I suppose.

20:30.463 --> 20:31.330
Sounds good to me.

20:31.330 --> 20:33.666
Good thinking, kid.

20:33.666 --> 20:36.567
But nothing alcoholic, okay?

20:40.273 --> 20:41.763
So...

20:42.041 --> 20:43.643
...here on the assault ship Basroil...

20:43.643 --> 20:46.479
...we survived our first campaign...

20:46.479 --> 20:48.572
...without any casualties.

20:49.615 --> 20:53.779
And I believe that survival is an
achievement worth celebrating.

20:58.758 --> 21:00.487
However...

21:00.693 --> 21:03.930
...the battlefield in which
we were just fighting...

21:03.930 --> 21:06.098
...was beginning to stir again.

21:06.098 --> 21:09.795
The machinery of war
was moving into action.

21:11.137 --> 21:15.775
Including the Aptic system,
the United Mankind dispatched...

21:15.775 --> 21:17.243
...missions to five planetary systems.

21:17.243 --> 21:20.780
It's not as though we've
destroyed them all.

21:20.780 --> 21:25.479
Yes. Our analysis shows we failed
to eliminate about half of them.

21:25.918 --> 21:28.716
The remaining ships probably
escaped with important information.

21:29.121 --> 21:30.656
That cannot be helped.

21:30.656 --> 21:34.760
However, reconnaissance missions
can be a double-edged sword.

21:34.760 --> 21:38.531
Surely we were able to learn
valuable information...

21:38.531 --> 21:40.726
...about the strength of their fleet.

21:41.200 --> 21:42.167
Absolutely correct.

21:42.602 --> 21:44.904
According to the analysis done by
the Communications Department...

21:44.904 --> 21:47.673
...the numbers of the
enemy fleet fall...

21:47.673 --> 21:50.733
...somewhere between 180
and 200 squadrons.

21:53.813 --> 21:56.213
Maybe I underestimated them.

21:56.816 --> 21:59.652
Let me consider this.

21:59.652 --> 22:01.721
I'll return to the bridge shortly.

22:01.721 --> 22:03.188
Very good, sir.

22:05.057 --> 22:07.727
The enemy appears to be
recovering quickly.

22:07.727 --> 22:12.562
It suggests that they had knowledge
about our plans for invasion.

22:12.832 --> 22:15.301
If that is not the case...

22:15.301 --> 22:19.205
...then it means that their
massive fleet in this area...

22:19.205 --> 22:21.639
...is only the tip of the iceberg.

22:21.874 --> 22:23.341
In any case...

22:25.778 --> 22:27.939
There's only one thing to do.

22:31.717 --> 22:33.886
The battle in which the Basroil
took part...

22:33.886 --> 22:37.413
...was only one
small part of the operation.

22:38.457 --> 22:40.826
As soon as we had finished
our first campaign...

22:40.826 --> 22:43.727
...and were ready for a
well-deserved rest...

22:44.230 --> 22:48.690
...Operation Phantom Flame
moved into the next phase.

22:54.240 --> 22:58.540
kizukanaikoto ga
The things I did not notice

22:59.278 --> 23:03.339
konnani takusan aru
I didn't know there were so many

23:04.684 --> 23:08.279
kyoumade no jibun ga
I think of myself until today

23:09.622 --> 23:13.319
nasakenaku omoete
To be so pathetic

23:13.459 --> 23:15.861
kuyashii kurai
It's almost frustrating

23:15.861 --> 23:19.558
haritsumeta kimochiga
This tense feeling

23:20.966 --> 23:26.105
massugu ni muite ireba
As long as I keeping facing forward

23:26.105 --> 23:29.666
setsunasa no nukumori
This momentary warmth

23:30.076 --> 23:34.069
hajimete shitta
I understood it for the first time

23:34.613 --> 23:39.251
kimi ga iruto
When you are there

23:39.251 --> 23:46.459
itsumo pink no namida ga nagareteru
The pink tears are always flowing

23:46.459 --> 23:51.697
kono mune no naka wo afureteru
My heart is brimming with it

23:51.697 --> 24:00.036
kimi ga dokoni itemo dareto hanashitemo
Wherever you are and whoever you talk to

24:02.007 --> 24:07.146
issho ni itaiyo soba ni ite
I want to be with you, to be near you

24:07.146 --> 24:12.551
tsunaida te kara yubisaki kara
From our joined hands and our finger tips

24:12.551 --> 24:20.925
karadajuu no omoi binetsu tsutawatte
My body heat transmits the feelings inside

24:21.360 --> 24:25.626
tomerarenai
And I cannot stop it

24:32.004 --> 24:33.973
Are they honorable?

24:33.973 --> 24:34.667
I think so.

24:35.608 --> 24:37.200
Lafiel?!

24:37.610 --> 24:41.910
I've heard people say his
Chief of Staff is also a Bebaus.

24:43.215 --> 24:46.514
I suppose you think you're
the paragon of common sense.

24:48.554 --> 24:51.523
Are you saying I haven't got any,
Nefee?

24:52.725 --> 24:55.421
We can have Admiral Bebaus
head up that fleet.

24:56.028 --> 24:57.863
A person with many loves
will not be promoted.

24:57.863 --> 25:01.390
Next episode...
Spectacular Insanity
